            "<p>First discovered site (1921)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Mohenjo-daro</p>",
            "<p>Great Bath and large granary</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Lothal</p>",
            "<p>Dockyard and maritime trade</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Kalibangan</p>",
            "<p>Evidence of ploughed field</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Dholavira</p>",
            "<p>Advanced water conservation system</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rakhigarhi</p>",
            "<p>Largest Harappan site in India</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "tn8ewmg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.Town Planning"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "rabxak8",
      "content": "• Cities were divided into Citadel and Lower Town"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "fiikap1",
      "content": "• Houses were made of baked bricks"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "jp38x7l",
      "content": "• Roads intersected at right angles"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0zjjqee",
      "content": "• Covered drainage system was highly advanced"
    },
    {
      "id": "e51922u",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "6.Economy"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "a1ma0mh",
      "content": "• Agriculture was the main occupation"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4g5o5jf",
      "content": "• Wheat and barley were major crops"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xmcrr4k",
      "content": "• Trade existed with Mesopotamia"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "mktmdzz",
      "content": "• Standard weights and measures were used"
    },
    {
      "id": "i4c8wmb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "7.Religion"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "layw8st",
      "content": "• Worship of Mother Goddess"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "0n8ol5r",
      "content": "• Pashupati seal suggests proto‑Shiva worship                                                     "
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "035oxjb",
      "content": "• Sacred animals included bull and unicorn"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g7mxm16",
      "content": "• Peepal tree considered sacred"
    },
    {
      "id": "dqgysp4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "8.Decline of the Indus Valley Civilization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5t7xvbx",
      "content": "• Climate change and drying of rivers"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z7daote",
      "content": "• Floods and natural disasters"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Major sites of the Indus Valley Civilization and their unique archaeological importance are frequently asked in SSC exams.",
        "Town planning features and economic aspects of the Harappan Civilization form recurring objective questions.",
        "Questions often focus on the key theories regarding the decline of the Indus Valley Civilization."
      ],
      "id": "0gh8lrm"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "pihdg9x",
      "content": "• Decline in trade"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "va1bh1c",
      "content": "• Possible Aryan migration theory (debated)"
    },
    {
      "id": "5vq7529",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9.SSC Exam Important Facts"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "dzyhrkd",
      "content": "• Indus Valley script is still undeciphered"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "8cssry3",
      "content": "• Lothal is famous for dockyard"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "s796jfs",
      "content": "• Dholavira is known for water management"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lx6guig",
      "content": "• Harappa civilization is also called Bronze Age civilization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "juidldq",
      "content": "• Great Bath is located in Mohenjo‑daro"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}